<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-include path="./_theme.mjml" />
    <mj-title>Player registration form</mj-title>
    <mj-preview><%= clubName %> — due before your first match on <%= firstFixture %></mj-preview>
  </mj-head>
  <mj-body background-color="#eef0f4" width="600px">

    <mj-include path="./_header.mjml" />

    <mj-section padding="28px 0 0">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text mj-class="kicker" text-transform="uppercase">Player registration</mj-text>
        <mj-text mj-class="h1" padding="6px 24px 0"><%= clubName %></mj-text>
        <mj-text mj-class="sub" padding="4px 24px 0">Season <%= seasonLabel %></mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section padding="16px 0 0">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text>Hello<%= greetingName %>,</mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          We have not yet received <%= clubName %>'s player registration form for the
          <%= seasonLabel %> season. Every player must be registered before they play,
          so please send it back before your first match.
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- The deadline block. mj-raw around the conditional: an EJS tag sitting directly
         between two MJML components is DISCARDED by the compiler, and whatever it guarded
         then renders unconditionally — so an "already passed" warning would show for
         every club. tools/build-emails.js counts the tags and fails if any were eaten. -->
    <mj-section padding="8px 0 0">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-raw><% if (overdue) { %></mj-raw>
        <mj-text mj-class="callout">
          <strong><%= clubName %>'s first match was <%= firstFixture %>.</strong>
          The form is overdue — please send it as soon as you can.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-raw><% } else { %></mj-raw>
        <mj-text mj-class="callout">
          <strong>Your first match is <%= firstFixture %><%= daysLine %>.</strong>
        </mj-text>
        <mj-raw><% } %></mj-raw>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section padding="16px 0 0">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text mj-class="h2">What to do</mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          The form is attached as a Word document, already filled in with the players we
          have on your teams. Add anyone missing, delete anyone who has left, then send it
          back to <a href="mailto:<%= replyTo %>"><%= replyTo %></a>.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-text>
          You can also keep your squads up to date on the website, which is where the
          attached list comes from.
        </mj-text>
        <mj-button href="<%= rosterUrl %>" css-class="cta">Manage your players</mj-button>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-include path="./_footer.mjml" />
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
